1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:06,590
Football Intelligence Platform is an AI football analytics project for
Europe's top five leagues.

2
00:00:06,940 --> 00:00:12,340
It pairs explainable match predictions with a grounded assistant and a
native Android app.

3
00:00:13,640 --> 00:00:22,140
Twenty-six seasons of results flow through a validated pipeline into an
XGBoost model, SHAP explanations and a goals model.

4
00:00:22,490 --> 00:00:27,910
One FastAPI backend serves them all, to the app and to the assistant
alike.

5
00:00:29,210 --> 00:00:35,550
The app is invite-only. A friend redeems a one-time code and chooses a
password.

6
00:00:35,900 --> 00:00:40,650
Then they accept a short notice that says exactly what the server
records.

7
00:00:41,950 --> 00:00:47,900
My Team follows a favourite club: its next match, the model's pick and
the reasons behind it.

8
00:00:48,250 --> 00:00:55,160
Below that, a season outlook: the projected finish, and the chance of
the title, the top four or relegation.

9
00:00:56,460 --> 00:01:01,740
Fixtures cover all five leagues, refreshed every day, with team crests.

10
00:01:02,090 --> 00:01:04,630
Tap any match to predict it.

11
00:01:05,930 --> 00:01:12,310
The result shows home, draw and away probabilities, and the most likely
scores from the goals model.

12
00:01:13,610 --> 00:01:21,220
Explain lists the factors behind the pick in plain football language,
from the SHAP values attached to every prediction.

13
00:01:22,520 --> 00:01:27,750
The assistant gives the same numbers, because it calls the prediction
service as a tool.

14
00:01:28,100 --> 00:01:33,380
It now runs on Cloudflare Workers AI and answers in about three seconds.

15
00:01:34,680 --> 00:01:40,820
Stop the server, and the app keeps working with the last data it saved,
under an offline banner.

16
00:01:42,120 --> 00:01:50,930
Behind it is a versioned FastAPI backend with OpenAPI docs, invite-only
sign-in, and liveness and readiness probes for hosting.

17
00:01:52,230 --> 00:01:57,490
Every request carries an ID, and every log line is structured JSON.

18
00:01:57,840 --> 00:02:04,750
One chat answer can be followed through its tool calls and its model
call, with tokens, cost and duration.

19
00:02:06,050 --> 00:02:11,470
It all runs on a laptop with no cloud, and the same image is ready for
Cloud Run.

20
00:02:11,820 --> 00:02:16,840
Tests, evaluations and every design decision are in the repository.
